# Slice 333 (the author 2026-11-09: `fn: prepared`, "в любой момент можем подставить заготовленную структуру ресиверу
# fn и это будет объявлением функции в namespace"): prepared is an ordinary Structure, written in the data part of main,
# with the field name and the other arguments of fn; `fn: prepared` supplies them by their names, and the receiver
# creates the function triple in the namespace of this traversal, where the traversal reaches it. Its data is the
# written data (calls) completed by the own fields of the body (last), by the one constructor of every form; prepared
# stays as written. Slice 334 (Codex review of 333): `fn: other prepared` gives the same Structure to the form with a
# separate name -- its field name is an ordinary field there -- and the data of other is completed the same way (last),
# its counters its own.
# M11 5v: prepared and its computed declarations live in main's own data.
# p_calls, p_fields and p_parts keep the original descriptor observations.
int: k 2
sub: main () (
    prepared:
        name: triple
        args:
            int: a
        return: int
        data:
            int: calls 0
        code: (calls := calls + 1; int: last a; return: last * 3 + k)
    fn: prepared
    fn: other prepared
    int: r1 0
    int: r2 0
    int: c1 0
    int: c2 0
    int: r3 0
    int: c3 0
    int: c4 0
)
    r1 := triple(5)
    r2 := triple(2)
    c1 := triple\data\calls
    c2 := triple\data\last
    r3 := other(3)
    c3 := other\data\calls
    c4 := other\data\last
k := 4
main()
int: r1 main\data\r1
int: r2 main\data\r2
int: c1 main\data\c1
int: c2 main\data\c2
int: r3 main\data\r3
int: c3 main\data\c3
int: c4 main\data\c4
int: p_calls main\data\prepared\data\calls
int: p_fields length(main\data\prepared\data)
int: p_parts length(main\data\prepared)
